/*!
@defgroup tmr
@ingroup mod_timer System Timer Module (TMR)
@brief Shared-counter compare timer module for the YTMicro SDK.

@details
The TMR module provides a 32-bit free-running up-counter together with four
32-bit compare channels per instance. Software can use the shared counter as a
time base, program one-shot compare events at absolute tick values, or build
periodic schedules by advancing compare values after each event.

@section tmr_features Key Features
- One shared **32-bit up-counter** per TMR instance.
- **Four compare channels** per instance for independent event scheduling.
- **8-bit prescaler** on the shared counter clock path.
- Optional **per-channel interrupt enable** on supported devices.
- **Debug-stop control** for freezing the counter while the core is halted.
- **Microsecond-to-tick conversion** helper based on the active prescaler and
  the functional clock reported by `clock_manager`.
- Instance count scales with the target device through `TMR_INSTANCE_COUNT`.

@section tmr_modes Supported Modes

| Mode | Primary APIs | Description |
|------|--------------|-------------|
| Shared counter time base | TMR_DRV_Init(), TMR_DRV_StartTimer(), TMR_DRV_GetCounterValue() | Run one free-running counter and read timestamps from `CNT`. |
| One-shot compare event | TMR_DRV_InitChannel(), TMR_DRV_ConfigChannel(), TMR_DRV_GetStatusFlags() | Trigger a channel event when the counter reaches one absolute compare value. |
| Periodic compare schedule | TMR_DRV_ComputeTicksByUs(), TMR_DRV_IncrementTicks() | Re-arm the next compare deadline by adding a relative tick interval after each event. |
| Optional compare interrupt | TMR_DRV_InitChannel() with `interruptEnable` | Generate an interrupt request on supported devices when the compare flag is asserted. |

@section tmr_arch Module Architecture

@verbatim
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                Application Code                 │
│          (calls TMR_DRV_* functions)           │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│          TMR Driver Layer (tmr_driver.h/c)      │
│  ● Instance-based API (TMR_DRV_Init, etc.)      │
│  ● Direct register programming for TMR          │
│  ● Optional tick conversion via clock_manager   │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│             TMR Peripheral Hardware             │
│        (PRS, CTRL, CNT, CH[n].CMP/INT)          │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
@endverbatim

@subsection tmr_arch_driver Driver Layer (tmr_driver.h)
Application code should use the public `TMR_DRV_*` functions declared in
tmr_driver.h. The driver resolves the instance base address internally through
`TMR_BASE_PTRS` and programs the hardware registers directly.

@subsection tmr_arch_shared Shared Counter Model
Every compare channel in one instance observes the same `CNT` register:
- Starting or stopping the timer affects **all channels** in that instance.
- The prescaler is shared by every compare channel.
- Compare values are absolute counter targets, not per-channel down-counters.

@section tmr_config Configuration Parameters

@subsection tmr_config_module tmr_config_t Fields
| Field | Type | Description | Default / Source |
|-------|------|-------------|------------------|
| clockSource | tmr_clock_source_t | Optional clock-source selector when `FEATURE_TMR_HAS_CLOCK_SELECTION == 1`. | Caller-defined |
| clockPrescaler | uint8_t | Prescaler register value; effective divisor is `clockPrescaler + 1`. | `0U` from TMR_DRV_GetDefaultConfig() |
| stopInDebugMode | bool | Freeze the shared counter while the core is halted in debug mode. | `false` from TMR_DRV_GetDefaultConfig() |
| startValue | uint32_t | Initial counter value written to `CNT`. | `0U` from TMR_DRV_GetDefaultConfig() |

@note TMR_DRV_GetDefaultConfig() initializes only the common fields above.
If the optional `clockSource` field exists in the current build, set it
explicitly before calling TMR_DRV_Init().

@subsection tmr_config_channel tmr_channel_config_t Fields
| Field | Type | Description | Default / Source |
|-------|------|-------------|------------------|
| channel | uint8_t | Compare channel index in the range `0 .. TMR_CH_COUNT - 1`. | Caller-defined |
| compareValue | uint32_t | Absolute compare tick written to `CH[channel].CMP`. | Caller-defined |
| interruptEnable | bool | Enable compare interrupt generation when `FEATURE_TMR_HAS_INTERRUPT_ENABLE_CONFIG == 1`. | Caller-defined |

@note No dedicated default helper is provided for `tmr_channel_config_t`;
callers are expected to initialize every field before use.

@subsection tmr_config_features Device Feature Macros
| Macro | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| TMR_INSTANCE_COUNT | Number of TMR peripheral instances available on the device. |
| TMR_CH_COUNT | Number of compare channels per instance. Typical value: 4. |
| TMR_CLOCK_NAMES | Functional clock identifiers used by TMR_DRV_ComputeTicksByUs(). |
| FEATURE_TMR_HAS_INTERRUPT_ENABLE_CONFIG | Enables the optional `interruptEnable` field in `tmr_channel_config_t`. |
| FEATURE_TMR_HAS_CLOCK_SELECTION | Enables the optional `clockSource` field in `tmr_config_t`. |

@section tmr_usage Usage Patterns

@subsection tmr_usage_basic Pattern 1: Basic Compare Event Setup
Configure one TMR instance, schedule a single compare event, and start the
shared counter.

@code{.c}
#define TMR_INST  (0U)
#define TMR_CH0   (0U)

tmr_config_t moduleConfig;
tmr_channel_config_t channelConfig;
uint32_t ticks;

TMR_DRV_GetDefaultConfig(&moduleConfig);
#if defined(FEATURE_TMR_HAS_CLOCK_SELECTION) && (FEATURE_TMR_HAS_CLOCK_SELECTION == 1U)
moduleConfig.clockSource = TMR_CLOCK_SYSTEM;
#endif
moduleConfig.clockPrescaler = 0U;
moduleConfig.startValue = 0U;
TMR_DRV_Init(TMR_INST, &moduleConfig);

if (TMR_DRV_ComputeTicksByUs(TMR_INST, 1000U, &ticks) == STATUS_SUCCESS)
{
    channelConfig.channel = TMR_CH0;
    channelConfig.compareValue = ticks;
#if defined(FEATURE_TMR_HAS_INTERRUPT_ENABLE_CONFIG) && (FEATURE_TMR_HAS_INTERRUPT_ENABLE_CONFIG == 1)
    channelConfig.interruptEnable = true;
#endif
    TMR_DRV_InitChannel(TMR_INST, &channelConfig);
    TMR_DRV_StartTimer(TMR_INST);
}
@endcode

@subsection tmr_usage_periodic Pattern 2: Periodic Compare Rescheduling
Use one compare channel as a periodic software tick source by clearing the
compare flag and advancing the deadline by a fixed number of ticks.

@code{.c}
#define TMR_INST        (0U)
#define TMR_PERIOD_CH   (1U)

static uint32_t g_periodTicks;

void TMR0_IRQHandler(void)
{
    if (TMR_DRV_GetStatusFlags(TMR_INST, TMR_PERIOD_CH) != 0U)
    {
        TMR_DRV_ClearStatusFlags(TMR_INST, TMR_PERIOD_CH);
        TMR_DRV_IncrementTicks(TMR_INST, TMR_PERIOD_CH, g_periodTicks);
    }
}

void TMR_SetupPeriodicEvent(void)
{
    tmr_channel_config_t channelConfig;

    if (TMR_DRV_ComputeTicksByUs(TMR_INST, 100U, &g_periodTicks) == STATUS_SUCCESS)
    {
        channelConfig.channel = TMR_PERIOD_CH;
        channelConfig.compareValue = g_periodTicks;
#if defined(FEATURE_TMR_HAS_INTERRUPT_ENABLE_CONFIG) && (FEATURE_TMR_HAS_INTERRUPT_ENABLE_CONFIG == 1)
        channelConfig.interruptEnable = true;
#endif
        TMR_DRV_InitChannel(TMR_INST, &channelConfig);
    }
}
@endcode

@subsection tmr_usage_counter Pattern 3: Shared Counter Timestamping
Use the shared counter as a lightweight timestamp source and reseed it when a
new timing window starts.

@code{.c}
#define TMR_INST  (0U)

uint32_t startTick;
uint32_t endTick;
uint32_t elapsedTicks;

TMR_DRV_SetStartValueCount(TMR_INST, 0U);
TMR_DRV_StartTimer(TMR_INST);

startTick = TMR_DRV_GetCounterValue(TMR_INST);
/* Perform the operation being measured here. */
endTick = TMR_DRV_GetCounterValue(TMR_INST);

elapsedTicks = endTick - startTick;
TMR_DRV_StopTimer(TMR_INST);
@endcode

@section tmr_api API Quick Reference

@subsection tmr_api_init Initialization & De-initialization
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| TMR_DRV_Init() | Program module-level counter settings for one TMR instance. |
| TMR_DRV_Deinit() | Reset the shared counter and all compare channels. |
| TMR_DRV_GetDefaultConfig() | Fill the common fields of `tmr_config_t` with safe defaults. |

@subsection tmr_api_channel Channel Compare Control
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| TMR_DRV_InitChannel() | Program one compare channel from a configuration structure. |
| TMR_DRV_ConfigChannel() | Write an absolute compare value and enable the channel. |
| TMR_DRV_EnableChannel() | Enable a previously configured compare channel. |
| TMR_DRV_DisableChannel() | Disable a compare channel. |

@subsection tmr_api_counter Counter Control
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| TMR_DRV_SetStartValueCount() | Write a new seed value into the shared counter register. |
| TMR_DRV_StartTimer() | Start the shared free-running counter. |
| TMR_DRV_StopTimer() | Stop the shared free-running counter. |
| TMR_DRV_GetCounterValue() | Read the current `CNT` register value. |

@subsection tmr_api_sched Time Conversion & Scheduling
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| TMR_DRV_ComputeTicksByUs() | Convert a microsecond interval to TMR ticks. |
| TMR_DRV_IncrementTicks() | Advance a compare deadline by a relative tick interval. |

@subsection tmr_api_status Status Flag Management
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| TMR_DRV_GetStatusFlags() | Read the raw status value of one compare channel. |
| TMR_DRV_ClearStatusFlags() | Clear the compare flag of one channel. |

@section tmr_notes Important Notes

@subsection tmr_notes_shared Shared Counter Semantics
- Every compare channel in one instance shares the same counter and prescaler.
- Starting, stopping, or reseeding the counter affects all channels in that
  instance simultaneously.
- Compare values are absolute `CNT` targets, so channel deadlines should be
  planned against the shared counter timeline.

@subsection tmr_notes_convert Tick Conversion Dependency
- TMR_DRV_ComputeTicksByUs() depends on `clock_manager` to query the current
  functional clock listed in `TMR_CLOCK_NAMES`.
- The conversion also depends on the prescaler currently programmed in `PRS`.
- The function returns `STATUS_ERROR` if the converted value exceeds the
  32-bit compare-register range.

@subsection tmr_notes_config Channel Configuration Behavior
- TMR_DRV_InitChannel() is the preferred first-time setup API when channel
  interrupt enable state must be configured together with the compare value.
- TMR_DRV_ConfigChannel() rewrites the channel control register to enable the
  channel, so use it for compare-value updates rather than for preserving
  interrupt-related configuration on devices that support `interruptEnable`.
- TMR_DRV_GetDefaultConfig() does not initialize the optional `clockSource`
  field when that field exists in the current build.

@subsection tmr_notes_periodic Periodic Scheduling Behavior
- Call TMR_DRV_ClearStatusFlags() before or together with the re-arm logic in
  the event service path.
- TMR_DRV_IncrementTicks() adds the requested interval to the current compare
  value. If that deadline is already in the past, the driver re-bases the next
  deadline on the current counter value instead.
- Delaying the reschedule operation introduces phase drift in periodic-event
  software loops.

@section tmr_integration Integration Guide

@subsection tmr_integration_files Compilation Units
The following source file must be added to the project build:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/tmr/tmr_driver.c
@endverbatim

@subsection tmr_integration_include Include Paths
Add the following directory to the toolchain include path:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/inc/
@endverbatim

@subsection tmr_integration_symbols Compile Symbols
No special compile-time symbols are required for this module. Device-specific
feature macros such as `FEATURE_TMR_HAS_INTERRUPT_ENABLE_CONFIG` and
`FEATURE_TMR_HAS_CLOCK_SELECTION` are supplied by the selected device headers.

@subsection tmr_integration_deps Dependencies
- @ref clock_manager — Required when using TMR_DRV_ComputeTicksByUs() to
  convert time units into compare ticks.

*/
